Subject: media: i2c: add a gaokun3 rear camera module selector

The MateBook E Go is built with one of two interchangeable rear camera
modules, a Samsung S5K3L6 at i2c address 0x10 or an OmniVision OV13B10 at
0x36. They sit on the same CCI bus, behind the same CSIPHY, on GPIO7 as reset
and on MCLK4, and the device tree cannot express "either": both nodes cannot
be enabled, because gpiolib hands a reset line to one consumer only -- the
driver that loses that race fails on -EBUSY rather than on the hardware it
does not have -- and the two drivers would fight over the rate of the single
MCLK.

Keep both sensor nodes disabled instead, and let this driver run the module's
power sequence once at boot, read the id registers of each candidate and
register only the node whose module answered. That node's sensor driver then
probes against an ordinary i2c client with the rails, the reset line and the
clock all to itself.

The device tree gives this node a "sensors" phandle list of the candidates and
the same supplies, clock and reset a sensor node carries; those are repeated
because the sequence has to run before either sensor driver exists.

The CCI adapter runs every message of a transfer on its own (cci_xfer() in
i2c-qcom-cci.c), so the id read is a register-address write followed by a
read, the same shape the sensor drivers use.
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
index 6438caf..46bdfc0 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -780,6 +780,18 @@ config VIDEO_S5K3L6XX
 	  This is a V4L2 sensor driver for Samsung S5K3L6XX 13M
 	  camera sensor with an embedded SoC image signal processor.
 
+config VIDEO_GAOKUN3_CAMERA_SELECT
+	tristate "Huawei MateBook E Go rear camera module selector"
+	depends on I2C && OF
+	help
+	  The Huawei MateBook E Go is shipped with one of two
+	  interchangeable rear camera modules, a Samsung S5K3L6 at i2c
+	  address 0x10 or an OmniVision OV13B10 at 0x36, wired to the
+	  same CCI bus, CSIPHY, reset line and MCLK. This driver powers
+	  the module once at boot and registers only the sensor node
+	  whose module answers, so that one device tree works with
+	  either module.
+
 config VIDEO_S5K3M5
 	tristate "Samsung S5K3M5 sensor support"
 	select V4L2_CCI_I2C
